@cc [owner:spolu,label:architecture] contract-review-portability
The action MUST accept a PR number in the caller's repository without requiring caller-local review
scripts, prompts, skills, a Node project, or `cc-check`. Review instructions and tooling MUST come
from the selected action revision.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security] contract-review-setup-source
Setup MUST NOT execute package scripts from the checkout being reviewed.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security] contract-review-delegated-execution
Requests delegated by `github-actions[bot]` may execute Codex only after the originating run's
human actor has been verified to have current repository write access.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:architecture] contract-review-node-runtime
Review setup selects the Node.js version in the action revision's `cc-check/.nvmrc` for both local
action checkouts and remote action invocations.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-captured-context
Review context MUST include the captured request, merge base, comparison files, existing inline
comments and review bodies, and passed action-tooling checks.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-validation-scope
Validation results for bundled action tooling MUST NOT be represented as validation of the
inspected PR.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-progress
Each workflow run MUST report progress in its own `Contract review (<run-id>)` commit status on the
inspected head, linked to that run. Concurrent runs MUST NOT overwrite one another's status.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:product] contract-review-progress-result
Statuses MUST distinguish running, completed, failed, and cancelled execution. Setup, Codex, or
publication failures MUST NOT report successful completion; success denotes a completed review
and MUST NOT imply approval of the PR.
